47900390625, 0.023223876953125, 0.028411865234375, -0.01218414306640625, -0.00959014892578125, -0.0025997161865234375, 0.0228118896484375, 0.00555419921875, -0.0089874267578125, 0.0307159423828125, -0.036865234375, 0.01708984375, 0.006053924560546875, -0.005489349365234375, 0.0186614990234375, -0.003814697265625, 0.040374755859375, -0.0005273818969726562, 0.054595947265625, 0.001636505126953125, 0.043060302734375, -0.00959014892578125, -0.0011529922485351562, -0.001438140869140625, -0.0160369873046875, 0.009246826171875, 0.0004811286926269531, -0.02044677734375, 0.022369384765625, 0.052825927734375, -0.0189361572265625, -0.0198516845703125, -0.02679443359375, 0.024810791015625, -0.020904541015625, 0.006465911865234375, 0.0477294921875, 0.033050537109375, -0.00045561790466308594, -0.033782958984375, -0.01149749755859375, -0.010711669921875, 0.01055908203125, -0.0269622802734375, 0.0181121826171875, -0.018310546875, -0.0233001708984375, -0.01392364501953125, -0.01043701171875, 0.031951904296875, 0.00955963134765625, -0.00994110107421875, -0.007747650146484375], "payload": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "text": "Large-scale image generation has advanced through improvements in data scale, quality, rebalancing, and recaptioning. However, conventional pipelines typically optimize task-specific datasets in isolation. The primary challenge lies not only in curating each task-specific corpus, but also in organizing heterogeneous supervision according to the dependencies among generative capabilities. We introduce a \\textbf{capability-driven data infrastructure} that integrates capability-specific supervision construction with capability-aligned curriculum scheduling. This infrastructure comprises three specialized yet interoperable data engines, each providing complementary relational supervision for text-image grounding, inter-image transformation, and image-knowledge association. Caption experts further align text-to-image (T2I) and editing supervision across tasks and levels of granularity. A multi-stage curriculum jointly evolves task composition, visual concept distribution, data quality, and image resolution in accordance with the dependency order of capability acquisition. Capability-aware evaluation completes the loop through targeted retrieval, expert construction, and gap-aware resampling. At scale, this framework curates a 440M-image T2I corpus, 120M editing pairs, and over 27M image-entity pairs. Leveraging this infrastructure, we train multimodal diffusion models from scratch at two scales, with 3B and 6B parameters, respectively. We conduct quantitative evaluation on CPI-Bench, as well as qualitative assessments across diverse text-to-image and editing scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate broad visual coverage, versatile rendering, and effective transfer across generative capabilities."}}